<article class="env-theorem" id="03OS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03OS">Theorem <span data-tag="03OS">59.18.8</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Definition <a href="/tag/03OL" data-tag="03OL">59.18.1</a>. On $\textit{PAb}(\mathcal{C})$ the functors $\check{H}^ p(\mathcal{U}, -)$ are the right derived functors of $\check{H}^0(\mathcal{U}, -)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By the Lemma <a href="/tag/03OR" data-tag="03OR">59.18.7</a>, the functors $\check H^ p(\mathcal{U}, -)$ are universal $\delta $-functors since they are effaceable. So are the right derived functors of $\check H^0(\mathcal{U}, -)$. Since they agree in degree $0$, they agree by the universal property of universal $\delta $-functors. For more details see Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03AU" data-tag="03AU">21.9.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>